<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm2d-taiyuan-2026-11-18 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>RETIMED 2026-11-19: FLOWN. Actual liftoff 2026-11-18T22:51:00Z (Wed 18 Nov 2:51 p.m. PST; 19 Nov 6:51 BJT). Xinhua and CCTV (via China News): Shijian-24 reached the planned orbit, Long March flight 678. LL2 Launch Successful, net precision Minute, orbit Sun-Synchronous (no altitude). Spaceflight Now completed feed Launch Success at 22:51:00Z. utc shifted +60 s from the 22:50:00Z NET; ECEF geometry unchanged. ILLUSTRATIVE, not flight data.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 2D / Shijian-24 (Taiyuan LC-9) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 17.00 s, kick 1.675 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.667, payload 314 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.9790-0.003657*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: Long March 2D (configuration 2, two-stage) (sim/vehicles/lm2d.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-2D TIMELINE mode: configuration-2 stage data (World Launch Vehicles 2nd ed. 2007 via huijiwiki) + SAST TYPICAL flight sequence (huijiwiki); all event times hard constraints. Typical sequence, not this flight&#x27;s.
ILLUSTRATIVE. FLOWN. Shijian-24, Long March 2D, Taiyuan Launch Complex 9. Actual liftoff 2026-11-18T22:51:00Z (Wed 18 Nov 2:51 p.m. PST; 19 Nov 6:51 BJT). LL2 Launch Successful, net precision Minute, orbit Sun-Synchronous (no altitude). Xinhua and CCTV: satellite reached the planned orbit; Long March flight 678. utc-shifted +60 s from the 22:50:00Z NET; sim not re-run.
Vehicle and stage data reused from the lm2d-jiuquan entry (vehicles/lm2d.json): configuration-2 masses and the SAST TYPICAL sequence via huijiwiki, S1 vacuum via the YF-20 ratio, verniers ASSUMED to run from S2 ignition to 705.1 s, 3.35 m fairing 860 kg ASSUMED, Cd transferred from the LM-3B fit. Event times are the typical sequence, not this flight&#x27;s. No altitude/range knots are published.
TARGET ASSUMED: 500 km circular. LL2 lists Sun-Synchronous Orbit with no altitude, so 500 km remains an assumption. Azimuth 188.65 deg is the mean bearing from the pad through the A5897/26 and A5898/26 Q-line centres (188.57 and 188.73 deg). No deploy time is published.
Target (see launch config): insertion 500 km, apoapsis 500 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 188.65 deg; payload 314 kg.
Pad: 38.863128N 111.589567E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-18T22:51:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (No payload-deploy time is published (LL2 payload and orbit Unknown). The SAST typical sequence lists separation at 737.1 s, but that time is not this flight&#x27;s, so it is not used.). From insertion T+705.1 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 94.62 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF end T+12059 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 499.94 km, osculating 499.2 x 501.0 km, i 95.407 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: Typical-sequence residual-propellant venting after separation is not modelled.</description>
